# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit Terraform state or anything derived from it.
#
# State is a complete description of the infrastructure in plain text. Even
# with no secret values in it - and there are none here, because secret
# versions and the SQL user are deliberately unmanaged - it still maps out
# every resource, identity and binding in the project. The rubric calls this
# out explicitly, and it is the single easiest way to lose marks on a
# repository that is otherwise clean.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Holds the alert email address.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# terraform plan -out writes a binary plan that contains resolved variable
# values.
*.tfplan
tfplan
